WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.640
What does trigonometry actually mean?

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.980
In Greek this red part means triangle.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.800
And the blue part means measure.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.040
Trigonometry, is one of the most feared topics in Mathematics.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:22.220
But in reality it is extremely simple. The meaning itself is so simple.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.380
It's just the measure of all the things possible in a triangle.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.540
That's all .

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.360
Let's consider a triangle, ABC.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.180
Let 'a' be the length of the side opposite Angle A.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.100
And similarly let 'b' and 'c' be the lengths of the sides

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.720
opposite Angles B and C respectively.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.720
Take a close look at the triangle.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.720
What all can be measured in this triangle?

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.880
We can measure the Angles: Angle A, Angle B and Angle C.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.780
Or find the lengths of the sides, which in this case are a, b ,and c.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.320
These are the only six things we deal with in trigonometry.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:11.320
Three size and three angles. Out of these six we are given a few and using

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.080
trigonometry we need to find the rest.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.500
It cannot be difficult. Actually it gets a bit simpler

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.880
as trigonometry generally deals with only one kind of triangle.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.380
A right angled triangle,

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.680
which is also referred to as a right triangle.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.120
This right triangle is right angled at this vertex.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.820
The good news is that one angle is known and only two remain.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.360
This one and this one.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.740
Let this angle be theta.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.460
This is the triangle we will be dealing with to cover most of our trigonometry.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.700
A triangle with an angle theta and a right angle.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:58.540
It doesn't have to be called theta, but that's what it is generally referred to as.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.520
But how these kind of triangles help us in real life?

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.500
How does trigonometry help us in real life?

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.920
Let's say Zen wants to find the height of this tree.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.940
He has to measure this length, which is the height.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:16.900
One way is to make an approximate guess.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.580
But a better way to find the height is by using trigonometry.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.960
Let's assume this distance is known to us.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.680
Remember, it's always easier to find the distance

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.740
or the length on the ground than finding the distance vertically.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:37.420
And we can find the approximate measure of this angle which is theta.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.320
With just these two pieces of information

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.460
Zen can find the height of this tree.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:47.280
Finding the height of a tree may not sound appealing to you,

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.300
but the next example surely will.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.360
This time Zen wants to find the height of a mountain.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.360
If this distance is known

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.360
and this angle is known,

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.960
then the height can easily be found out.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:06.780
But how? That's precisely what we will try to understand in trigonometry.

